<!-- Hi3798Mv100 32bit Debian 13 full flash - maxmem edition - v1.0 (2026-10-02)
     All 9 partitions are Sel="1".

     Fixes included in this release:
     1. Vendor kernel rebuilt with CONFIG_FRAMEBUFFER_CONSOLE so fbcon drives
        the HDMI output.  Previously the kernel had /dev/fb0 but no fbcon,
        so console=tty0 produced nothing and HDMI stayed black.
     2. hifb now publishes a real fb_var_screeninfo (1920x1080-32bpp) before
        register_framebuffer(), so fbcon binds a colour 240x67 console instead
        of the mono fallback.
     3. hifb DRV_HIFB_ResetLogoState() drains pending freeLogoMemWork via
        cancel_work_sync() before memset()-ing gs_stLogo.  Without it the async
        work queued from DRV_HIFB_Open -> DRV_HIFB_CloseLogo had work->func
        zeroed and kworker jumped to NULL (process_one_work+0x34, address
        00000004), halting the boot before login.
     4. mmz tuned to mmz=ddr,0,0,48M (CMA 48M, reserve 215M) so both CMA and the fastboot reserve region fit.
     5. consoleblank=0 added to the kernel command line, so the console is
        never blanked after 10 minutes of keyboard inactivity.

     Kernel: hi_kernel-mv100-32-fbcon.bin
             md5 f9790e40b817f5fd587b54725b37acb0 (10,740,379 bytes) -->
